{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1469238-how-gothic-is-you-game","id":1469238,"title":"How Gothic is you Game?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-11-30T01:40:52-08:00","id":1469238,"title":"How Gothic is you Game?","content":"Sometimes in those threads of ours someone reminds us of the Punk in Punk Gothic. The struggle against The Man and all that.<br /> <br /> But I notice a lot of trends in the posts that are pretty much against the other side of this coin, the Gothic. Where are the Gothic tropes? The themes of the genre?<br /> <br /> Maybe most people here are used to the Gothic <i>aesthetics</i>, and think it kind of stops at that. Or that <b>Gothic = Dark and Brooding</b>. But me, I'm a huge fan of <b><i>Gothic Literature</i></b>, a complex genre with a long history that predates black and leather by quite some centuries.<br /> <br /> A genre about the nature of evil and the importance of choice. About villains with mundane dreams and fears, made dangerous by obsession and pride and plagued by the consequences of their actions. About temptation and Free Will, where redemption depends but on making the right choice, and accept the price of doing what's right instead of what's convenient.<br /> <br /> There was a reason Golconda wasn't so elusive in 1st edition. I don't think it should be. I don't think everyone and everything should be corrupt. Gothic isn't Grimdark and Grimdark is childish (on purpose, by the way, it does not take itself seriously, not when well done).<br /> <br /> I said in another thread some of the principles of the Gothic genre. Moralism, yes, but of a Humanist tone and through a naturalist lens. Evil isn't sin against God, but against other people, imprudence begets catastrophe and evil is self-punishing. Choice matters. Past behavior is predictive of future behavior. You reap the fruits of what you do. Change is hard, but never impossible. But denying it is easier than accepting responsibility.<br /> <br /> What others think of it? How do you understand the Gothic part of the game and how do you play by it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-30T03:21:21-08:00","id":1469240,"title":"","content":"I lock my PCs in a forcefield prison colony and force them to mine ore - that's how Gothic it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-30T03:35:15-08:00","id":1469242,"title":"","content":"I find myself agreeing with much of what you say but I've never actively sought to make my games &quot;Gothic&quot;. Rather I avoid romantic notions and make my setting cold and hard and uncomfortably close to reality. I fill my settings with lies. The truth will set you free, but it's very hard to find. Systems exist to benefit the people who create them. Golconda, or even becoming human again, is an escape route few will want you to take.<br /> <br /> But I think getting humanity 10 is... not a prerequisite to any kind of true enlightenment. I realy like the Gnostic view that reality's a prison because it makes such an interesting setting, and conforming to the expectations of a higher power in order to find forgiveness is paradoxical when said higher power has built such a nasty prison. Humanity 10 may certainly get you a kind of enlightenment, but removing yourself from the Jyhad is a self-serving goal without much higher purpose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 11-30-2021, 06:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-30T03:59:35-08:00","id":1469244,"title":"","content":"I've been in quite a few games and none of them could be defined gothic, most of the games I played (oWoD, CoD and V5) were street level and more akin to noir sensibilities, dark and gritty yes but definitely not grimdark. Personally I think that requiem is better equipped to make a &quot;lighter&quot; game since it lacks masquerade edgelord metaplot and the fact that the all night society is marginally better than the oWoD kindreds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-30T04:23:17-08:00","id":1469245,"title":"","content":"Gothic as fuck, bleak cities full of cold grim people, decadence and horror all around. I even make a point of implying the world is subtly worse than ours even without vampires.<br /> Conversely I tend to downplay the aspects of punk which are juvenile, shallow or nihilistic. Maybe that's why i find the anarchs are the least interesting of the big three.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-30T05:22:12-08:00","id":1469247,"title":"","content":"Anarchs are the least interesting of the big three. That's just fact. The Independents are more Punk. <br /> <br /> I think the world being darker than ours is a great literary device for satire. Satire is the golden sauce of god that should be spread evenly across the meal of any setting that mirrors the real world. Whether you play something seriously but bring it to the forefront like corruption or you play up something horrifying for laughs (my police have been very trigger happy of late) it's all fair so long as it's <i>true</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-30T05:40:50-08:00","id":1469248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1469238-how-gothic-is-you-game?p=1469242#post1469242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rather I avoid romantic notions and make my setting cold and hard and uncomfortably close to reality. I fill my settings with lies. The truth will set you free, but it's very hard to find. Systems exist to benefit the people who create them. Golconda, or even becoming human again, is an escape route few will want you to take.<br /> <br /> But I think getting humanity 10 is... not a prerequisite to any kind of true enlightenment. I realy like the Gnostic view that reality's a prison because it makes such an interesting setting, and conforming to the expectations of a higher power in order to find forgiveness is paradoxical when said higher power has built such a nasty prison. Humanity 10 may certainly get you a kind of enlightenment, but removing yourself from the Jyhad is a self-serving goal without much higher purpose.</div> </div> </div> </div>Although the Gothic genre is romantic, I don't find it contrary to a certain level of realism. Rather, I think its notion of how someone can suffer consequences for one's own actions more realistic than some people expect, and certainly more than the notion of karma.<br /> <br /> I also like the notion that truth will set you free, but instead of being hard to find it's just hard to accept. Which isn't necessarily counter to gnosticism. If enlightenment comes from experience rather than teaching, it doesn't mean it is too cryptic, but because it demands assuming one's own responsibilities.<br /> <br /> But I didn't get what you mean about Humanity 10. Although related, Humanity indeed isn't enlightenment. To decide to do no evil isn't the same as to decide to do good upon the world, or even upon yourself. It is a safe choice, as is to leave the Jyhad. It would only mean something in the context of a greater goal, a choice to action instead of inaction.<br /> <br /> This reminds me of two of my own characters, the Gaia worshiper Salubri and the Sabbat Tzimisce Doctor. Both had high Humanity, one actively seeking ways to improve the living of others and the cause of her faith, the other trying to avoid problems, pretend callousness and deliberately choosing actions that he could use to justify not risking his hold on the Beast. She was a Golconda seeker, possibly with a chance. He was just a coward, no matter how competent at his farce (and he was quite).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1469238-how-gothic-is-you-game?p=1469244#post1469244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been in quite a few games and none of them could be defined gothic, most of the games I played (oWoD, CoD and V5) were street level and more akin to noir sensibilities, dark and gritty yes but definitely not grimdark. Personally I think that requiem is better equipped to make a &quot;lighter&quot; game since it lacks masquerade edgelord metaplot and the fact that the all night society is marginally better than the oWoD kindreds.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree on parts and you did well to remind me that maybe most takes on the setting are more <i>Noir</i> than <i>Grimdark</i>. Although <i>Noir</i> isn't as realistic as some think, either.<br /> <br /> But I have to disagree in the sense that Gothic isn't necessarily lighter. Not at all. In fact, many Gothic stories only have a possibility of light to contrast the tragedy of the situation, the relevant characters locked in a torment of their own device without hope of escape, not because it is impossible, but because you <b>now</b> they won't make the choices they should.<br /> <br /> Can an elder vampire keep a high Humanity? If your answer is yes, and the reality is yet that none in your setting did it, because while they fear Wassail they also don't want to let their power and prestige go, and they prefer to repeat the lies that this is impossible or there are other means, just to not confront their own failures... this is Gothic. Heroes are possible, but not a necessity, and in fact most of the genre has none.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1469238-how-gothic-is-you-game?p=1469245#post1469245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Conversely I tend to downplay the aspects of punk which are juvenile, shallow or nihilistic. Maybe that's why i find the anarchs are the least interesting of the big three.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see a Big Three. That was a bad decision in V5, to extricate the Anarchs from the Camarilla. They're meant to be two sides of the same coin.<br /> <br /> The Punk and the Tyrant exist by and for the System, and the System is made of the Whole of the People. Even if the Tyrant sets the System for their own gain, there's only a System because the People buy into it. They are all together in it, and only this gives them meaning. The nuCam is the Tyrant over nothing because they expelled the People, the Anarchs are rebels without a cause because they have no System to rebel against. And Punks don't like rebels without a cause.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-30T06:13:17-08:00","id":1469249,"title":"","content":"I think that what makes most kindreds unlife miserable isn't the beast itself (although thats a pretty big factor) but the fact that the enviroment they live in is objectively horrible, most kindreds are left to fend for themself with few actually getting any kind of guidance, they have to default to survival mode and this only makes controlling the beast all the more difficult. The thing I dislike most about masquerade is ironically what makes the setting so popular, the whole kindred society is so dark and flatout evil that it borders on cartoonish at times, their whole structure was so flawed that a big masquerade breach was only a matter of time and the fact that v5 finally aknoweldged it, is one of its greatest selling points. The gothic aspect you are talking about were never a thing in masquerade despite marketing itself as a gothic game, the setting was much more fatalistic, utterly devoid of hope and just flatout horrible that it fell square on the grimdark side of things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-30T08:41:35-08:00","id":1469254,"title":"","content":"Now that I think of it, I probably never had a Gothic campaign, and seeing your pitch, I'd definitely like to play one.<br /> <br /> My own campaigns (both tabletop and the LARP sections that I manage) are usually of the political horror type: I'm not very solid on romanticism as a narrative tool, unfortunately. I also run action-oriented scenes and campaigns (of the pulp, high-ended tier). <br /> <br /> When I go into horror I usually delve into Body Horror or something mildly allucinatory (especially with the Underworld, credits to a friend of mine who is a frequent Storyteller and player with me, she is a huge fan of David Lynch and other similar authors).<br /> <br /> My WOD, or at least the WOD that comes out in my stories, is something between &quot;<i>House of Cards</i>&quot; (the English version) and &quot;<i>Berserk</i>&quot;, I'd say.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-30T10:17:43-08:00","id":1469260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1469238-how-gothic-is-you-game?p=1469249#post1469249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that what makes most kindreds unlife miserable isn't the beast itself (although thats a pretty big factor) but the fact that the enviroment they live in is objectively horrible, most kindreds are left to fend for themself with few actually getting any kind of guidance, they have to default to survival mode and this only makes controlling the beast all the more difficult. The thing I dislike most about masquerade is ironically what makes the setting so popular, the whole kindred society is so dark and flatout evil that it borders on cartoonish at times, their whole structure was so flawed that a big masquerade breach was only a matter of time and the fact that v5 finally aknoweldged it, is one of its greatest selling points. The gothic aspect you are talking about were never a thing in masquerade despite marketing itself as a gothic game, the setting was much more fatalistic, utterly devoid of hope and just flatout horrible that it fell square on the grimdark side of things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kindred society didn't had to be as bad as you paint it before Revised. Indeed, it runs against the necessities put forth by Humanity. I won't say the game don't have parts that work that way (it has plenty), but it definitely isn't the whole of it.<br /> <br /> To say it fell square on Grimdark... some supplements aside I not only disagree but can objectively point out a lot of text on many books against it. That may be the setting as used by many, but definitely not the setting as written. It may not be as Gothic as I would like (it isn't, its focus is more Punk), but it isn't Grimdark.<br /> <br /> And given that it keeps the <i>status quo</i> of the Masquerade untouched save for the SI and makes all factions more simplistic and antagonistic to mortals, I do not see V5 as an improvement in that regard, definitely it didn't acknowledge any big Masquerade breach whatsoever, if much it recognizes the Masquerade as unbreakable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1469238-how-gothic-is-you-game?p=1469254#post1469254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now that I think of it, I probably never had a Gothic campaign, and seeing your pitch, I'd definitely like to play one.</div> </div> </div> </div>The two tips I can think of now to give you.<br /> <br /> First, think about what your characters really want. Not their goals, but their desires, that which makes them happy. Love, respect, family, peace. Some may desire power, those that find power itself intoxicating, but want is different from desire, most covet power as a means to have the lives they picture for themselves.<br /> <br /> Second, picture how the natural consequences of their actions keep them from achieving those true desires, either by keeping them out of reach or by tarnishing them to an undesirable state. The character may hold to a number of beliefs that justify their actions and make them unable to see how they are sabotaging themselves, or may even see their own desires as a flaw, denying themselves out of pride.<br /> <br /> An example would be a character that wants true friendship, but believes that only by achieving a high position they'll have the respect and attention necessary to make meaningful friends. Then just run in your mind the story of the character sacrificing relationships, making compromises with foes, and generally becoming and amassing around themselves the exact kind of people they despise.<br /> <br /> Remember that &quot;true desires&quot; in this context are simple, but deep. They are the root cause of your beliefs, not the beliefs themselves. Frequently they are unconscious and they may be ill-defined, this is not a problem, as long as you can see the character setting the circumstances to make themselves miserable.<br /> <br /> Let them free at the end to make others miserable as they lash out to the world, working their plans and beliefs, indulging their pride, and, secretly even to themselves, dumping their frustration on others. Know desires, let consequences run their course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-30T12:34:59-08:00","id":1469266,"title":"","content":"You call the SI getting reactivated not a masquerade breach? all the world's governments are aware of kindreds now and hellbent on their destruction, the fact that they kept it quiet to the public at large doesn't mean that the masquerade isn't now broken on a fundamental level.<br /> As far as punk go, I think that is more of an anarch theme that comes with a fundamental difference between the oWoD anarchs and the v5 ones, the first were rebelling against the camarilla for treating them like shit and the whole movement was focused on tearing it down while still having a structure remarcably similar (baron or prince, semantics really) who treats kindreds only marginally better than the camarilla, the punk there was more aesthetic than idealistic since the anarchs still very much believed in the masquerade and in someone holding power over others (again baron and prince) while also not really caring about human society. The v5 anarch cater to modern American sensibilities making anarchs paragons of social justice and using them to insert themes and thematics that cather to a certain audience, giving them actual punkish ideals, still, not something that would really define the vampire ip since the archetypal game is about a bunch of bitches doing their sires bidding, often without understanding the full picture and taking the brunt of a cold, uncaring world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-30T15:00:46-08:00","id":1469271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1469238-how-gothic-is-you-game?p=1469260#post1469260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kindred society didn't had to be as bad as you paint it before Revised. Indeed, it runs against the necessities put forth by Humanity. I won't say the game don't have parts that work that way (it has plenty), but it definitely isn't the whole of it.<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>As a rule of thumb I tend to consider opting out of vampiric society as much as possible the correct move for vampires.<br /> One of the hidden merits of the carmarilla in 3rd was the potential for a vampire to minimise interactions with others. It was perfectly plausible assuming the prince wasn't mind stupid to be left to your own devices as long as you respect the masquarade once you have an established domain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 11-30-2021, 06:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-30T15:14:49-08:00","id":1469272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1469238-how-gothic-is-you-game?p=1469247#post1469247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anarchs are the least interesting of the big three. That's just fact.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pfft.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:18px\">How Gothic is my World of Darkness?</span><br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://geekandsundry.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/06/vpg.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></b><br /> <br /> Very.<br /> <br /> I personally think the Gothic element of V:TM is more prevelant than the punk element. Yes, there's a lot of conflict between the Anarchs and the Elders, the young and the old, and the rich versus the poor but the game doesn't necessarily force you into the position of the underdog. You can side with the decadent Toreador, the ultra-wealthy Ventrue, or the duplictious Tremere just as well as the other side. This is a Gothic Punk game where, if it was a cyberpunk game, you could also be a corporate agent as well as the plucky underdog.<br /> <br /> The way I handle V:TM is that the cities are divided between the decaying slums and the gleaming towers. That the Camarilla is full of inbred decadent and corrupt old fossils that are always plotting against one another because it is literally the entirety of the point of their existence. There's all sorts of hidden secrets, terrible abuses, and tragic pasts. I encourage all of my players to have melodramatic PAIN and ANGST.<br /> <br /> My vampire society is full of <i>Eyes Wide Shut</i> parties, childer abused by their sires, secret affairs, deals with the Devil, corruption, and unspeakable drama across family lines/bloodlines. Guilt and horror at what you are constant themes with almost no vampire not suffering some existential horror at the bleakness of their existence and filling the void with lust, power, hate, or pleasure.<br /> <br /> I mean, if you're a vampire, you have almost certainly committed some horrible unforgivable act that haunts your nightmares. I encourage all of my players to have some terrible guilt from the Hunger or tragic backstory: abusive sire, dead family, murderous frenzy, or something else that is a terrible secret. Kindred society is built on tragic romances, obsessions, seduction, envy, revenge, and murderous jealousy. Every Kindred is obsessed with these larger than life emotions and willingness to break every taboo.<br /> <br /> Kindred are romantic and tragic as well as horrifying as well as disturbed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 11-30-2021, 06:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-30T22:48:54-08:00","id":1469290,"title":"","content":"Honestly it upsets me to think there's a &quot;big three&quot; and that anarchs qualify. <br /> <br /> Honestly, in most cities, I think the Camarilla have won and there's peace and prosperity between cooperative vampires (at the expense of mortals) Child-sire relationships are mutually beneficial and clans act as family in most cases. <br /> <br /> True punk isn't the Brujah trying to tear down the system, True Punk is playing an archetypal Ventrue that strives for order and peace and subtly shifting mortal society so that ample numbers of people fit his feeding criteria: Victims of domestic violence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-01T00:00:30-08:00","id":1469293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1469238-how-gothic-is-you-game?p=1469290#post1469290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly it upsets me to think there's a &quot;big three&quot; and that anarchs qualify.<br /> <br /> Honestly, in most cities, I think the Camarilla have won and there's peace and prosperity between cooperative vampires (at the expense of mortals) Child-sire relationships are mutually beneficial and clans act as family in most cases.<br /> <br /> True punk isn't the Brujah trying to tear down the system, True Punk is playing an archetypal Ventrue that strives for order and peace and subtly shifting mortal society so that ample numbers of people fit his feeding criteria: Victims of domestic violence.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like this pretty much show why the Anarchs and you don't get along. The Camarilla is not peaceful, it is not prosperous, and it is a constant violent game of upheaval and manipulation.<br /> <br /> If you think it's utopian of noble lords who treat their peasants well, of course there's not a seething peasant rebellion.<br /> <br /> If a vampire tells his family about the Masquerade, a Ventrue Prince can:<br /> <br /> A. Erase their memory and chastise them.<br /> B. Stake the vampire and leave him out for the Sun.<br /> C. Take his family to be horribly murdered and/or drained by the Elders of the court as an example.<br /> <br /> A may be smartest but C certainly is the better story.<br /> <br /> In RL, dictators tend to be assholes. Why would the Beast make them less so?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 12-01-2021, 03:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-01T00:04:30-08:00","id":1469294,"title":"","content":"All vampires are lords, some are just mightier than others. The peasants are the ghouls and the swathes of humans. <br /> <br /> Also like, peasant rebelions weren't that common because lords usually knew their limits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-01T00:10:15-08:00","id":1469295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1469238-how-gothic-is-you-game?p=1469294#post1469294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All vampires are lords, some are just mightier than others. The peasants are the ghouls and the swathes of humans.<br /> <br /> Also like, peasant rebelions weren't that common because lords usually knew their limits.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's another reason why they don't work for you. If you don't think of the Anarchs as the poor and impoverished of vampiredom then you're not going to think of them as justified in doing everything they can to revolt.<br /> <br /> But even if they were, history is absolutely full of civil insurrection and war against lesser feudal lords to bigger ones.<br /> <br /> Basically, your position is, &quot;Why burn down Paradise?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-01T00:33:36-08:00","id":1469296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1469238-how-gothic-is-you-game?p=1469293#post1469293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel like this pretty much show why the Anarchs and you don't get along. The Camarilla is not peaceful, it is not prosperous, and it is a constant violent game of upheaval and manipulation.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">If a vampire tells his family about the Masquerade, a Ventrue Prince can:</span></span></span><br /> A. Erase their memory and chastise them.<br /> B. Stake the vampire and leave him out for the Sun.<br /> C. Take his family to be horribly murdered and/or drained by the Elders of the court as an example.<br /> <br /> A may be smartest but C certainly is the better story.<br /> <br /> In RL, dictators tend to be assholes. Why would the Beast make them less so?</div> </div> </div> </div>1: The Camarilla is the most prosperous sect by a good few miles. Only the Giovanni might beat them per-capita, but it's very easy to understate how fucking <i>loaded </i>the camarilla are. Rather than concerning yourself with how prosperous the camarilla is, you should consider how decadent their wealth and power makes them.<br /> <br /> 2: B is typically the smartest. C goes against the purported ideals of the Camarilla (humanity is good and y'all shouldn't cause more trouble than necessary in the name of the masquerade). A is really the option you'll take as a compromise if the city's political makeup makes the prince concerned about the political ramifications of option B.<br /> <br /> <br /> 3: In RL, Dictators are smart fellows that keep the right people with the right amount of power: Enough to keep them happy, not enough to entertain a coup. They might be assholes to the powerless populace, but they're typically very generous with friends and friends of friends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 12-01-2021, 05:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-01T03:42:36-08:00","id":1469300,"title":"","content":"I think you're both a little extreme on this but to me the issue isnt the camarilla is good or bad, it's that anarchs are too threadbare to carry the setting as they're expected to in v5. They really do work better as a dissident movement within the ivory tower were the lack of coherance or ideology is forgivable, I think were V5 really runs into trouble is with the anarch book were the brave new anarch world has nothing going on except someone ghouling babies<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Back on subject how Gothic are the anarchs? Personally I've always thought the camarilla/sabbat carried the goth with anarch being the punk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-01T03:49:20-08:00","id":1469301,"title":"","content":"doublepost.sorry","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 12-01-2021, 06:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-01T04:09:18-08:00","id":1469303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1469238-how-gothic-is-you-game?p=1469266#post1469266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You call the SI getting reactivated not a masquerade breach?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. I do. Any problem with that?<br /> <br /> For me it is <i><b>a</b> Masquerade <u>breach</u></i>, indeed, but not <b><i>the</i></b><i> Masquerade <b><u>break</u></b></i>. The Masquerade is not nearly as harmed as I think it should be. Period.<br /> <br /> Otherwise we discussed the matter on other threads. Let's wait for the SI book to know the degree to which the governments actually know something and then we can discuss such a premise.<br /> <br /> Also, please use double enter on your posts. They're hard to read due to lack of spaces.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1469238-how-gothic-is-you-game?p=1469266#post1469266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as punk go, I think that is more of an anarch theme that comes with a fundamental difference between the oWoD anarchs and the v5 ones</div> </div> </div> </div>I thoroughly disagree with your description as it seems to me to come from a biased reading on both versions of the Anarchs. Both are more varied than that yet each you chose to assume one PoV and discard others.<br /> <br /> By the way, Punk isn't equal to social justice. There are a lot of ways to cater to social justice without being punk.<br /> <br /> The game <u><b>does</b></u> have posers and sellouts, on both versions, and certainly the Punk movement is against it. But that's exactly why the game have posers and sellouts, to act as foils to true Punks in the Anarchs.<br /> <br /> What changed is that in V5 those posers and sellouts have a lot more power and influence, since they are the ones commanding (or trying to) Anarch cities.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1469238-how-gothic-is-you-game?p=1469272#post1469272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Every Kindred is obsessed with these larger than life emotions and willingness to break every taboo.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would like to emphasize the role of choice in the Gothic genre. Vampires do not have a choice on being vampires, so they can't be unavoidably evil. This is a key concept, as the Gothic heavily applies the discourse of damnation as a way for the evil character to justify themselves. But what actually damn them is their choices, not their nature.<br /> <br /> Again, that's why 1st edition had Golconda <i>relatively</i> easy to achieve. It was an indication that salvation was less a mysterious choice and more a <b>hard</b> choice. The possibility of achieving it is an important contrast to the villain's unwillingness to do so, as doing so would meant recognizing one's error.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1469238-how-gothic-is-you-game?p=1469300#post1469300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you're both a little extreme on this</div> </div> </div> </div>Thoroughly agree.<br /> <br /> I don't think the Camarilla is either always smart and fair with vampires, or that it is the ultimate depiction of tyranny. Both would weaken the setting as possibilities.<br /> <br /> Also, both readings are punk. The game is both Punk Lit and open for Punk characters, so the oppression over mortals and Ghouls is important, but the plight of the Anarchs is also true. First 'cause many are indeed oppressed, second because some want to ease the plight of mortals.<br /> <br /> Of course, as a Punk game it must have things the Punks hate, posers and sellouts in their midst, so as a <i>movement</i> the Anarchs aren't as Punk as the aesthetics they adopt.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1469238-how-gothic-is-you-game?p=1469300#post1469300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They really do work better as a dissident movement within the ivory tower</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much that, one way or the other. Punk is about oppression and fighting The Man. A city without The Man is a place without a need for Punks. It may be anarchist (arguably), but not Punk.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1469238-how-gothic-is-you-game?p=1469300#post1469300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Back on subject how Gothic are the anarchs? Personally I've always thought the camarilla/sabbat carried the goth with anarch being the punk.</div> </div> </div> </div>In terms of aesthetics I mostly agree, although the two can mix well, sometimes.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, I think they all play into the interrelations that define both genres. While the Punk needs The Man, The Mass and The Rebel, the Gothic needs The Monster, The Victim and The Witness. There's always a witness in the Gothic literature, that sometimes doubles as Hero if the work does have a hero.<br /> <br /> So while they obviously may all be used interchangeably in specific stories, as a whole they also always fill an important role. The Anarchs are The Rebel and The Witness, the Camarilla is The Man and The Monster, the Sabbat has a more flowing role where it can be anything, despite its overt obsession with being The Monster and never The Victim.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-01T08:15:32-08:00","id":1469317,"title":"","content":"I'm honestly curious as to what would constitute a masquerade break for you since apparently you think that the SI reforming with all the world's governments backing and clearing out London of all vampire presence while also burning the Vienna chantry to the ground is merely a masquerade breach but you are right, lets wait for the SI book to clarify things (even if I think that things are plenty clear already).<br /> <br /> My vision of the anarchs is biased yes, I always found them a puerile attempt at having a medium to insert real world issues in the game and cater to certain players that want to play vampire superheroes (superheroes with fangs anyone), that is perfectly fine of course since all the players should have the means to play their own game (which is one of the main reasons why I prefer requiem over masquerade, sandbox rules). If you are interested in using punk or gothic themes in your game just do so, there is plenty of material to go around, especially in v5, me I prefer my vampires to be bloodsucking monsters who couldn't care less about human problems because they are dealing with plenty of shit already, this kind of thinking doesn't go well neither with punk nor gothic but fits really well with noir sensibilities and most of the games I had went into this direction. Should I ever run a game of v5, the anarch barons and camarilla princes would be a case of &quot;same shit different flavour&quot;, both would be powerhungry assholes who throw young licks to their final death without a second thought, the PC struggles would be to cater to their whims while struggling to keep what little humanity they have left.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-01T08:55:32-08:00","id":1469323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1469238-how-gothic-is-you-game?p=1469317#post1469317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm honestly curious as to what would constitute a masquerade break for you since apparently you think that the SI reforming with all the world's governments backing and clearing out London of all vampire presence while also burning the Vienna chantry to the ground is merely a masquerade breach but you are right, lets wait for the SI book to clarify things (even if I think that things are plenty clear already).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><b>The Second Inquisition 1.5</b><br /> <br /> I think Onyx Path Publishing has actually done a good deal to &quot;course correct&quot; what was originally presented as something that was ill-thought out and that the version presented in Chicago by Night and later Jason Carl is something that is much more reasonable for the game. I also suspect that Justin Achilli will be formally &quot;correcting&quot; the version presented in THE CAMARILLA that was itself different from the Core Book.<br /> <br /> The Second Inquisition has been retconned multiple times officially too with THE FALL OF LONDON being the biggest one. Originally, it was presented as a display of how thoroughly awesome and terrifying the SI was and how the most powerful city in the world for the Camarilla could be brought down by mortals.<br /> <br /> The adventure module changed things significantly so it was instead a story about how the SI was unable to open a jar of pickles without Mithras to do it for him and that they only got as far as they did with him opening the backdoor for them to every Kindred in London's haven and paying for their guns with his cult. The SI had unlimited authority and the support of the government because, well, a 4th generation vampire used his thousands of years old secret society to let them have it and it was only for about a few weeks before they lost it.<br /> <br /> The OPP version and one Jason Carl used in LA by Night that seems to be similar to the one in the comic book is that the SI is actually just the exact same groups of hunters that existed in The Hunters Hunted. They've just allied together and now have a lot of support from a few very important patrons (like the fucking NSA) that are willing to bail them out. There's a bit of vampire supremacy going on as well since the Mausoleum attack was orchestrated by Lazarus/Japeth/The Capuchin and is more or less Mithras and London 2.0. The Mexico attack seems to have also been either taken advantage of or helped with by Fiorenza.<br /> <br /> Vienna has no secret vampire mastermind but, well, we're all thinking it does.<br /> <br /> I did like one thing that THE CAMARILLA presented, though, which was the fact the important thing to remember about the SI is they think the war is OVER. That they won in Vienna, the vampires are decapitated and are now in &quot;mopping up&quot; stage with no more need for a big war. This is, IMHO, probably a &quot;Mission Accomplished&quot; parody and the vast majority of funding and favors done for them are going to dry up now.<br /> <br /> The way I do is the show NARCOS. The SI has some truly dedicated incredibly fanatical hunters out to destroy all vampires everywhere but their patrons are already bored with it and weary of, &quot;If I just had X more money and weapons, I could wipe out the vampire race/drugs.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My vision of the anarchs is biased yes, I always found them a puerile attempt at having a medium to insert real world issues in the game and cater to certain players that want to play vampire superheroes (superheroes with fangs anyone), that is perfectly fine of course since all the players should have the means to play their own game (which is one of the main reasons why I prefer requiem over masquerade, sandbox rules). </div> </div> </div>Modern issues in a punk game set in an exaggerated dark version of the real world! Goodness gracious me!<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you are interested in using punk or gothic themes in your game just do so, there is plenty of material to go around, especially in v5, me I prefer my vampires to be bloodsucking monsters who couldn't care less about human problems because they are dealing with plenty of shit already, this kind of thinking doesn't go well neither with punk nor gothic but fits really well with noir sensibilities and most of the games I had went into this direction. Should I ever run a game of v5, the anarch barons and camarilla princes would be a case of &quot;same shit different flavour&quot;, both would be powerhungry assholes who throw young licks to their final death without a second thought, the PC struggles would be to cater to their whims while struggling to keep what little humanity they have left. </div> </div> </div>Ironically, you're describing punk. Punk and noir are distinctly related styles and the latter influenced the former. Part of the issue is that a lot of people are familiar with Punk as a musical concept but rarely punk as a literary genre. A fundamental misunderstanding of the punk ideology is the belief that they're trying to make things better. Nihilism is an inherent quality of punk with the general belief that improvement may be impossible but that doesn't mean you shouldn't be angry as fuck.<br /> <br /> Mark Rein Hagen, who is the guy who CREATED the Anarchs, absolutely 100% intended the Anarchs to be &quot;same shit, different toilet&quot; with Juggler as the first Anarch leader (and first Anarch period) and being almost identical to the Kindred Prince Modius. They're both manipulative assholes who kidnapped beautiful women to be their enslaved childer.<br /> <br /> The Anarchs are not the GOOD GUYS in all of this but the philosophy is correct for the setting. Which is to say the players are probably going to be Anarchs. Not because they want to be but because they will rebel against the Camarilla, Princes, and structures of the system--and that includes other Anarchs. Which is to say your player characters are probably anarchs even if they think the Anarchs are a bunch of stupid assholes. Just because they are trying to forge their own independence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 12-01-2021, 12:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-01T09:15:42-08:00","id":1469324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1469238-how-gothic-is-you-game?p=1469317#post1469317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm honestly curious as to what would constitute a masquerade break for you since apparently you think that the SI reforming with all the world's governments backing and clearing out London of all vampire presence while also burning the Vienna chantry to the ground is merely a masquerade breach but you are right, lets wait for the SI book to clarify things (even if I think that things are plenty clear already).</div> </div> </div> </div>The SI reforming with all the world's government's backing is so ridiculous it can't be taken at face value. Strikes me as very much &quot;Chicken little&quot; with someone seeing a problem and assuming the most extreme worst case cause. The SI book will likely dial it down several thousand notches. But this is really beyond the scope of this thread. <br /> <br /> <br /> Actually related to this thread<br /> Goth and Punk subcultures don't really exist anymore, beyond a few guys in their 60's failing to adjust. It is interesting watching both V20 and V5 humouring such a bygone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-01T09:23:06-08:00","id":1469325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1469238-how-gothic-is-you-game?p=1469323#post1469323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Anarchs are not the GOOD GUYS in all of this but the philosophy is correct for the setting. Which is to say the players are probably going to be Anarchs. Not because they want to be but because they will rebel against the Camarilla, Princes, and structures of the system--and that includes other Anarchs. Which is to say your player characters are probably anarchs even if they think the Anarchs are a bunch of stupid assholes. Just because they are trying to forge their own independence.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is probably because your Camarilla is the most extreme case of stupid-evil and your chronicles probably drive your players into rebelling. In all the games I've played, I've only seen one Anarch defector (from the Giovanni might I add) Every player that starts Camarilla stay Camarilla, at most flirting with the Anarchs. The players who start Anarch tend to be be... erm... noobs. Their character concepts are often dumb and they die quick (this isn't when I'm GMing BTW, it's not my doing!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-01T09:23:36-08:00","id":1469326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1469238-how-gothic-is-you-game?p=1469324#post1469324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually related to this thread<br /> Goth and Punk subcultures don't really exist anymore, beyond a few guys in their 60's failing to adjust. It is interesting watching both V20 and V5 humouring such a bygone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Part of why Paradox is so international is they're alive and well....just not in America that just seemed to collectively say they were over in the 2000s.<br /> <br /> But Europe and South America?<br /> <br /> Huge.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-01T09:35:29-08:00","id":1469327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1469238-how-gothic-is-you-game?p=1469325#post1469325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>This is probably because your Camarilla is the most extreme case of stupid-evil and your chronicles probably drive your players into rebelling.</b> In all the games I've played, I've only seen one Anarch defector (from the Giovanni might I add) Every player that starts Camarilla stay Camarilla, at most flirting with the Anarchs. The players who start Anarch tend to be be... erm... noobs. Their character concepts are often dumb and they die quick (this isn't when I'm GMing BTW, it's not my doing!)</div> </div> </div> </div>That is an outright <i>bizarre</i> statement to make. No, seriously, I'm kind of confused. If I'm the Storyteller and want to do an Anarch game then of course the Camarilla is going to be tyrannical. If the Prince and the Primogen aren't a bunch of assholes then why would there be an Anarch Movement at all? You're acting like the players being driven into the Anarchs is a personal failing when it's just the premise of a lot of games. It's like going, &quot;The Empire is so stupid evil! It's like you want the Rebellion to rebel!&quot;<br /> <br /> The thing is that I'm usually illustrating the worst side of the Camarilla in my games because we're discussing Anarchs. The funny thing that I have actually done a lot of games where the Prince is very reasonable: when the PCs are the Prince.<br /> <br /> My games are inherently political and once you manage to overthrow the tyranny, the real fun begins of having to deal with the fact that you will be under constant threat by stupid assholes who don't realize how much of a danger they are to mortals or other Kindred (Anarchs) and Camarilla who perceive being a reasonable moderate Prince as a sign of weakness. Part of what I loved about doing the TRANSYLVANIA CHRONICLES with my longtime players was that I had them as Prometheans as well as longtime radical proto-Anarchs.<br /> <br /> And I made the Camarilla the apex of attempted reforms and building a better Kindred society versus what had existed before--with the implication that if it ever fell, what replaced it would be so much worse.<br /> <br /> Or to paraphrase, &quot;The problem with Kindred society isn't the government, it's the people.&quot;<br /> <br /> I admit one of the best Anarch games I ever did was where the PCs successfully overthrew the Prince, made a deal with the new one, and protected the city from a Sabbat attack--only to be immediately backstabbed by their former Anarch allies who were jealous of their success.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-01T09:37:01-08:00","id":1469328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1469238-how-gothic-is-you-game?p=1469326#post1469326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Part of why Paradox is so international is they're alive and well....just not in America that just seemed to collectively say they were over in the 2000s.<br /> <br /> But Europe and South America?<br /> <br /> Huge.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Are you talking about videogames? because I assure you that here in Italy I have yet to find someone who plays world of darkness or chronicles, as far as videogames goes I can think of Europa and of course Bloodlines 2 (If they manage to release it thats it), I have friends in France and Germany and they say its more or less the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-01T09:46:09-08:00","id":1469329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1469238-how-gothic-is-you-game?p=1469328#post1469328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you talking about videogames? because I assure you that here in Italy I have yet to find someone who plays world of darkness or chronicles, as far as videogames goes I can think of Europa and of course Bloodlines 2 (If they manage to release it thats it), I have friends in France and Germany and they say its more or less the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>Weird, because I belong to an Italian Facebook World of Darkness group.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-01T09:48:17-08:00","id":1469331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1469238-how-gothic-is-you-game?p=1469323#post1469323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>The Second Inquisition 1.5</b><br /> <br /> I think Onyx Path Publishing has actually done a good deal to &quot;course correct&quot; what was originally presented as something that was ill-thought out and that the version presented in Chicago by Night and later Jason Carl is something that is much more reasonable for the game. I also suspect that Justin Achilli will be formally &quot;correcting&quot; the version presented in THE CAMARILLA that was itself different from the Core Book.<br /> <br /> The Second Inquisition has been retconned multiple times officially too with THE FALL OF LONDON being the biggest one. Originally, it was presented as a display of how thoroughly awesome and terrifying the SI was and how the most powerful city in the world for the Camarilla could be brought down by mortals.<br /> <br /> The adventure module changed things significantly so it was instead a story about how the SI was unable to open a jar of pickles without Mithras to do it for him and that they only got as far as they did with him opening the backdoor for them to every Kindred in London's haven and paying for their guns with his cult. The SI had unlimited authority and the support of the government because, well, a 4th generation vampire used his thousands of years old secret society to let them have it and it was only for about a few weeks before they lost it.<br /> <br /> The OPP version and one Jason Carl used in LA by Night that seems to be similar to the one in the comic book is that the SI is actually just the exact same groups of hunters that existed in The Hunters Hunted. They've just allied together and now have a lot of support from a few very important patrons (like the fucking NSA) that are willing to bail them out. There's a bit of vampire supremacy going on as well since the Mausoleum attack was orchestrated by Lazarus/Japeth/The Capuchin and is more or less Mithras and London 2.0. The Mexico attack seems to have also been either taken advantage of or helped with by Fiorenza.<br /> <br /> Vienna has no secret vampire mastermind but, well, we're all thinking it does.<br /> <br /> I did like one thing that THE CAMARILLA presented, though, which was the fact the important thing to remember about the SI is they think the war is OVER. That they won in Vienna, the vampires are decapitated and are now in &quot;mopping up&quot; stage with no more need for a big war. This is, IMHO, probably a &quot;Mission Accomplished&quot; parody and the vast majority of funding and favors done for them are going to dry up now.<br /> <br /> The way I do is the show NARCOS. The SI has some truly dedicated incredibly fanatical hunters out to destroy all vampires everywhere but their patrons are already bored with it and weary of, &quot;If I just had X more money and weapons, I could wipe out the vampire race/drugs.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Modern issues in a punk game set in an exaggerated dark version of the real world! Goodness gracious me!<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Ironically, you're describing punk. Punk and noir are distinctly related styles and the latter influenced the former. Part of the issue is that a lot of people are familiar with Punk as a musical concept but rarely punk as a literary genre. A fundamental misunderstanding of the punk ideology is the belief that they're trying to make things better. Nihilism is an inherent quality of punk with the general belief that improvement may be impossible but that doesn't mean you shouldn't be angry as fuck.<br /> <br /> Mark Rein Hagen, who is the guy who CREATED the Anarchs, absolutely 100% intended the Anarchs to be &quot;same shit, different toilet&quot; with Juggler as the first Anarch leader (and first Anarch period) and being almost identical to the Kindred Prince Modius. They're both manipulative assholes who kidnapped beautiful women to be their enslaved childer.<br /> <br /> The Anarchs are not the GOOD GUYS in all of this but the philosophy is correct for the setting. Which is to say the players are probably going to be Anarchs. Not because they want to be but because they will rebel against the Camarilla, Princes, and structures of the system--and that includes other Anarchs. Which is to say your player characters are probably anarchs even if they think the Anarchs are a bunch of stupid assholes. Just because they are trying to forge their own independence.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Wait, are you telling that now I have to follow a webseries instead of the core book to get what its going on? what happened to erratas?<br /> <br /> <br /> Regarding modern issues in the game, I am not opposed to that since they are necessary for worldbuilding but making them central? no thank you, I am a blood sucking monster of the night, I really don't care about the next American elections or whatever fad got the American pubblic (mostly because I'm not American and I don't understand half of the stuff they are talking about).<br /> <br /> <br /> Regarding anarchs, we have different views, I've never been in a game where the PC flocked to the anarchs to &quot;get their independence&quot; if anything most anarch were either the power angry pricks I wrote before or a bunch of young, angry and utterly useless morons whose days were numbered in the single digits, either way, the last people I would turn to gain independence from the camarilla, besides, If I wanted to play an easily triggered dipshit I would have played werewolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","user":"Newb95","date":". 12-01-2021, 02:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-01T09:50:47-08:00","id":1469332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1469238-how-gothic-is-you-game?p=1469329#post1469329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Weird, because I belong to an Italian Facebook World of Darkness group.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There is plenty of fan pages and groups, I'm talking about real gaming, all I found is Dnd and some Pathfinder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-01T10:45:45-08:00","id":1469335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1469238-how-gothic-is-you-game?p=1469328#post1469328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Are you talking about videogames? because I assure you that here in Italy I have yet to find someone who plays world of darkness or chronicles, as far as videogames goes I can think of Europa and of course Bloodlines 2 (If they manage to release it thats it), I have friends in France and Germany and they say its more or less the same.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ehy, fellow Italian!<br /> <br /> VtM is not as zeitgeisty as it was in the 90s, of course, but it has become again widely available on the italian market - I can buy manuals in my local LEGO store (it would be fun to see CULTS OF THE BLOOD GODS one shelf after LEGO Fairy Farm).<br /> <br /> I also had no big troubles finding online VtM groups, and there were V5 tables at every RPG event I attended or that I saw recently. Need Games is doing a good job (it might get stronger on community support, compared to some other games it has, perhaps, but they were precise and consistent in their publishing schedule).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-01T10:54:54-08:00","id":1469336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1469238-how-gothic-is-you-game?p=1469335#post1469335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Ehy, fellow Italian!<br /> <br /> VtM is not as zeitgeisty as it was in the 90s, of course, but it has become again widely available on the italian market - I can buy manuals in my local LEGO store (it would be fun to see CULTS OF THE BLOOD GODS one shelf after LEGO Fairy Farm).<br /> <br /> I also had no big troubles finding online VtM groups, and there were V5 tables at every RPG event I attended or that I saw recently. Need Games is doing a good job (it might get stronger on community support, compared to some other games it has, perhaps, but they were precise and consistent in their publishing schedule).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What region are you from? I'm from campania and at my local gaming shop nobody knew about V5, I bought the manual on Need Games but I've yet to find a group online let alone in the real world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-01T10:56:57-08:00","id":1469337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1469238-how-gothic-is-you-game?p=1469290#post1469290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly it upsets me to think there's a &quot;big three&quot; and that anarchs qualify.<br /> <br /> Honestly, in most cities, I think the Camarilla have won and there's peace and prosperity between cooperative vampires (at the expense of mortals) Child-sire relationships are mutually beneficial and clans act as family in most cases.<br /> <br /> True punk isn't the Brujah trying to tear down the system, True Punk is playing an archetypal Ventrue that strives for order and peace and subtly shifting mortal society so that ample numbers of people fit his feeding criteria: Victims of domestic violence.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I've played only in a few Anarch games, most of my games were Camarilla: but a prosperous city in which the Camarilla has won and peace reigns ... well, there's definitely less room for action than a troubled one. Especially in LARPs, competition and factional struggle between Camarilla PCs and their allies were always the moving factor of the chronicle, and much more efficient at delivering plot and emotions than some external enemy coming to trouble the well-oiled machinery of a cooperative Camarilla.<br /> <br /> The Camarilla shouldn't be tyrannic just for the sake of it: but the Elders are scared of the young, who crave their blood and wealth, and they're also creatures whose Humanity has been eroded by centuries. They are also able to enforce their will by using supernatural powers and blood addiction, so they are uniquely positioned to be ... well, assholes!<br /> <br /> A mortal dictator lives a far more complicated life than a Vampire oligarch - and at least in theory he doesn't have a bloodthirsty monster raging in his stomach.<br /> <br /> Camarilla is surely prosperous but it deals in very limited and compllicated resources - blood: it's not like most Camarilla princes maintain Welfare States who provide subsdized blood to their subjects, if they are lucky they can compete with others in a relatively huge Rack, otherwise Domains are locked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12590,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","user":"Manfr","date":". 12-01-2021, 02:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-01T10:58:38-08:00","id":1469338,"title":"","content":"7<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1469238-how-gothic-is-you-game?p=1469336#post1469336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> What region are you from? I'm from campania and at my local gaming shop nobody knew about V5, I bought the manual on Need Games but I've yet to find a group online let alone in the real world.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm from Marche, near Ancona: there's always been quite a lot of LARPs here, so we've had a stable VtM community so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-01T11:04:10-08:00","id":1469340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1469238-how-gothic-is-you-game?p=1469338#post1469338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">7<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm from Marche, near Ancona: there's always been quite a lot of LARPs here, so we've had a stable VtM community so far.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Lucky you, aside from Dnd and some pathfinder my town seems like a desert.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-01T11:05:03-08:00","id":1469341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1469238-how-gothic-is-you-game?p=1469260#post1469260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The two tips I can think of now to give you.<br /> <br /> First, think about what your characters really want. Not their goals, but their desires, that which makes them happy. Love, respect, family, peace. Some may desire power, those that find power itself intoxicating, but want is different from desire, most covet power as a means to have the lives they picture for themselves.<br /> <br /> Second, picture how the natural consequences of their actions keep them from achieving those true desires, either by keeping them out of reach or by tarnishing them to an undesirable state. The character may hold to a number of beliefs that justify their actions and make them unable to see how they are sabotaging themselves, or may even see their own desires as a flaw, denying themselves out of pride.<br /> <br /> An example would be a character that wants true friendship, but believes that only by achieving a high position they'll have the respect and attention necessary to make meaningful friends. Then just run in your mind the story of the character sacrificing relationships, making compromises with foes, and generally becoming and amassing around themselves the exact kind of people they despise.<br /> <br /> Remember that &quot;true desires&quot; in this context are simple, but deep. They are the root cause of your beliefs, not the beliefs themselves. Frequently they are unconscious and they may be ill-defined, this is not a problem, as long as you can see the character setting the circumstances to make themselves miserable.<br /> <br /> Let them free at the end to make others miserable as they lash out to the world, working their plans and beliefs, indulging their pride, and, secretly even to themselves, dumping their frustration on others. Know desires, let consequences run their course.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you, I will start from here to re-visit my Tremere one shot set in the collapse of the Pyramid: wonderful ideas! Tremere are also very gothic in their themes, so I think they will fit.<br /> <br /> Touchstones seems to be a useful tool in the context of a Gothic game, even though they are a bit difficult to use meaningfully in a single-session game, unless it's based on them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-01T14:32:13-08:00","id":1469359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1469238-how-gothic-is-you-game?p=1469331#post1469331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> besides, If I wanted to play an easily triggered dipshit I would have played werewolf.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>Yeah, this is uncalled for. Please take a warning and don't insult other gamelines or their players.</b></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-01T14:50:49-08:00","id":1469363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1469238-how-gothic-is-you-game?p=1469359#post1469359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>Yeah, this is uncalled for. Please take a warning and don't insult other gamelines or their players.</b></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You misunderstood, I didn't insult anyone, I am a werewolf player too &quot;when will you rage&quot; that the best (and funniest) part of the game and I was drawing comparison between the average anarch mook and the archetypal high rage garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-01T15:00:07-08:00","id":1469364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1469238-how-gothic-is-you-game?p=1469331#post1469331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding modern issues in the game, I am not opposed to that since they are necessary for worldbuilding but making them central?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, making them central is a declared goal of the game in its every incarnation. But you already made it clear you don't like it and don't like either main genres, that's perfectly fine.<br /> <br /> I would like, though, that you don't call games that cater to social issues in derisive terms. That's unnecessary. Personally I'm not a fan of true <i>noir</i>, yet I'm not calling names on it despite being a popular take.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1469238-how-gothic-is-you-game?p=1469326#post1469326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Part of why Paradox is so international is they're alive and well....just not in America that just seemed to collectively say they were over in the 2000s.<br /> <br /> But Europe and South America?<br /> <br /> Huge.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are caveats, but yes.<br /> <br /> It's important to remember that both literary movements are very dynamic and can exist in many forms and shapes. They're also especially fertile to seed others. <i>Noir</i> itself is an example (already old, of course) of derived genre from both.<br /> <br /> But dead? They're among the most alive genres, despite a decline in the turn of the century. A huge number of media genres are subgenres to one of those two, as are many subcultures and a lot of people still cling to the main branches while giving audience to the sub-branches.<br /> <br /> Punk never became mainstream, and that's part of what makes it seems it is dead. The innate animosity towards posers since its inception makes Punk marginalized by definition, yet never dead, always present.<br /> <br /> Gothic did became mainstream and seeded larger culture far and wide. A <b>huge</b> amount of movies, series, books, comics and whatnot are <i>extremely</i> Gothic even when they don't say it out loud. Gothic played straight, parodied, deconstructed, reconstructed, reskinned, re-reskinned, Mixed with other genres, all the forms of Gothic you want.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1469238-how-gothic-is-you-game?p=1469341#post1469341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Touchstones seems to be a useful tool in the context of a Gothic game, even though they are a bit difficult to use meaningfully in a single-session game, unless it's based on them.</div> </div> </div> </div>They surely are. Indeed, that's what they tried to do with the draconian rules for <i>harming</i> and <i>destroying</i>. The rules may be toned down, but their current form is exactly what a Gothic villain would assume.<br /> <br /> And that's also why Touchstones are people. I don't personally think they <i>have</i> to be, but in a Gothic game most would anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-02T09:26:34-08:00","id":1469404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1469238-how-gothic-is-you-game?p=1469240#post1469240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I lock my PCs in a forcefield prison colony and force them to mine ore - that's how Gothic it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah? Well, I force my PCs to into the rolls of the 1986 British psychological horror film directed by Ken Russell (starring Gabriel Byrne as Lord Byron, Julian Sands as Percy Bysshe Shelley, Natasha Richardson as Mary Shelley, Myriam Cyr as Claire Clairmont and Timothy Spall as Dr. John William Polidori. That\u2019s Gothic my game is!<br /> <br /> Joking aside, how Gothic something is in a game will depend on a lot of factors. Describing a city or the setting of a scene in lavish detail - a Gothic literature wallows in detail - will slow a game too much, and make it boring for the players. Likewise Gothic traditions often involve isolation will the VtM game involves a lot of socializing. I do make the WoD a dour and unforgiving place, and the pleasant manners of the Camarilla just a coat of paint over awefulness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-02T10:06:06-08:00","id":1469407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1469238-how-gothic-is-you-game?p=1469404#post1469404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Describing a city or the setting of a scene in lavish detail - a Gothic literature wallows in detail - will slow a game too much, and make it boring for the players. Likewise Gothic traditions often involve isolation will the VtM game involves a lot of socializing.</div> </div> </div> </div>But Gothic may and do indulge in socialization, as long as it isn't crowded. And the game expects vampiric population to be limited. Even metropolises have between 50 and 200 Kindred at most, many cities have just a handful.<br /> <br /> Of course, it isn't so obvious when you get the world-spanning conspiracies and sect conflicts of the full metaplot, but by most core descriptions you get that the bulk of Kindred society live in small, closed, incestuous circles, where you see the same faces over and over for decades.<br /> <br /> The standard setting is a city with a few dozen vampires and so little direct contact with the outside that visitors are an event on themselves. This is pretty Gothic. And the details you leave for props, something the game always encouraged, because here you got a point, but this is more of a media limitation than a genre contradiction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-02T11:44:32-08:00","id":1469410,"title":"","content":"Punk: Inequalities of power, Slums, Homelessness, predators vs. prey, modern nobility, gleaming towers, and rusted ruined factories<br /> <br /> Gothic: Tragic lover affairs, guilt, redemption, sin, horrible curses, abusive sires, creepy mansions, and madness","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-02T15:13:55-08:00","id":1469420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1469238-how-gothic-is-you-game?p=1469363#post1469363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You misunderstood, I didn't insult anyone, I am a werewolf player too &quot;when will you rage&quot; that the best (and funniest) part of the game and I was drawing comparison between the average anarch mook and the archetypal high rage garou.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>Please don't argue with mods. I got what you were saying. We don't appreciate the use of triggered that way.</b></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-02T15:18:46-08:00","id":1469422,"title":"","content":"It occurs to me Sabbat are probably the best faction for both goth and punk. Which is pretty amusing considering how they got downplayed this ed","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-02T16:15:30-08:00","id":1469429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1469238-how-gothic-is-you-game?p=1469422#post1469422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It occurs to me Sabbat are probably the best faction for both goth and punk. Which is pretty amusing considering how they got downplayed this ed</div> </div> </div> </div>I admit I tend to play Sabbat as mocking the whole Goth thing. They revel in their evil, feel no guilt, and could not care less about damnation. They love being monsters and all it cost them was everything.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-02T17:42:15-08:00","id":1469447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1469238-how-gothic-is-you-game#post1469238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What others think of it? How do you understand the Gothic part of the game and how do you play by it?</div> </div> </div> </div>There was a brief article from White Wolf Magazine back in the 90s that explained what the Gothic and Punk parts of the World of Darkness's Gothic-Punk setting was supposed to involve, and I rather wish some version of it had been included in the revised edition of Vampire. But it ended up having a sizable influence on how I viewed the World of Darkness. <br /> The Gothic part is, obviously, the Gothic fiction genre of the Romantic movement, but also all of the stuff that influenced it and was influenced by it. One of those influences is medieval Gothic architecture, with its large and imposing buildings that are meant to convey a sense of power and permanence, especially of the Church and other political powers that be. This combination of age, size, and power tends to give off a mood of oppression, and of people's inherent weakness within the world's greater scheme of things. The sins of the past weight heavy on the present, in the forms of long standing corruption, family curses, ancient feuds and hatreds, and even ones own past personal mistakes and failings.<br /> And this should be personal to the characters. The fact that the world they inhabit is ancient and mysterious in ways that they will likely never fully understand should weigh on them. The awareness that for all their power as one of the Kindred, they are still in danger. That what they have is fleeting. Perhaps even their sanity and humanity. <br /> And ultimately, this should make them angry as well as terrified or heartbroken. This is the where the Punk aspect comes in. The need to rebel against the above. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-03T00:35:21-08:00","id":1469468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1469238-how-gothic-is-you-game?p=1469422#post1469422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It occurs to me Sabbat are probably the best faction for both goth and punk. Which is pretty amusing considering how they got downplayed this ed</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, every Gothic story needs a Monster, and every Punk story has some weirdo booster skinheads bothering you \ud83d\ude01<br /> <br /> Speaking more seriously, as CT Phipps has said, the Sabbat takes pride in being monstrous: it's very fit for Gothic stories, but I think it's better suited as either the Villain you are facing, or the monstrous Abyss in which you gaze, only to be changed into something terrible. <br /> <br /> As for Punk, the Sabbat is very fitting for stories about the dehumanising side of radicalism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-03T02:02:41-08:00","id":1469474,"title":"","content":"As I said, the Sabbat is in a state of flux in this regard. Many of them were victimized in some way inside or outside the sect, many of them try to stand for their fellows in some sense, and many of them, as monstrous as they are try to fight worse things than them, and they may be right.<br /> <br /> It adds nuance that Paths are so varied. Many are optional monsters instead of obligatory monsters. Not all, certainly, but many are. They have their own hypocrites in spades, too, but also a fair number of zealots. Shovelheads are finally a wild card, as you can't predict how the survivors will develop.<br /> <br /> But I don't think they're better fitted to the genres, they're just another color for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-03T15:31:47-08:00","id":1469533,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ve always been interested in learning about the theory and academic thought for things, both because I think it\u2019s cool and I believe it helps me better understand the subject I\u2019m reading/hearing about (or at least, more peoples perspectives on it).<br /> <br /> That said, I\u2019ve also always loved stereotypical goth aesthetics. Whether the trenchcoat, black lace, &amp; urban grunge aesthetics of the 90s or the Victorian Gothic aesthetics or the crumbling castles and universal horror/hammer horror shows. I was always fascinated by horror hosts and Halloween specials and all that kind of stuff. So, on one level, I do also just enjoy the aesthetics for what they are, even if they can be overwrought or cartoony at times.<br /> <br /> I also agree though that Gothic themes can be useful in so many more ways for storytelling then just an eye catching pastiche. For one thing, one of the genres most commonly associated with many peoples vision of what modern vampire should be, something inspired by American Noir &amp; Noir-inspired espionage and political thrillers, is arguably inspired by the earlier tradition of Gothic stories amongst pulp fiction and penny dreadfuls as well as full horror literature. Gothic horror is even more explicit as the arguable ancestor of the modern horror genre as it stands, in general.<br /> <br /> That being said, it makes sense then that one can imagine how the concepts derived from an analysis of gothic horror could be useful for vampire. I\u2019ll go with just a few which I recall from reading:<br /> <br /> \u2022Comic-Horror Paradigm<br /> Some analysts would argue that, rather then tragedy, horror serves better as the dramatic counterpart to comedy. The reasoning being is that, if the core of comedy is a paradigm of fertility (the misadventures of lovers, unquenchable thirst for life, slapstick medical logic, relentless spirit, the flush of liveliness and traditionally the promise that at the end of the story the young lovers are married with children) then horror as a paradigm of sterility and decay serves as the natural opposite (familiar bodies begin to slip apart and slide undone, terrible forces haunt the protagonists, what should be good and safe becomes dark and dangerous, the productive forces of life flag and eventually fail, the young lovers are separated by death without consumption of their union). This concept becomes useful for storytelling as not only does it allow comedy to be played with and close at hand but offers principles to shape the horror of the situation: the inevitable decay of familiar matter, the fragility of living beings, the collapse into sorrow, the failure of productive forces, and the tragic non-completion of the comedic ideal.<br /> <br /> \u2022Contemporary Anachronism <br /> Another concept that gothic horror plays with is the idea that while the present moment is fragile and fleeting, the past is eternal and ever present. The past is ever present in the gothic consciousness, even when it ought to be gone: the classic images of ghosts, vampires, and decrepit estates demonstrate that easily enough. The point still stands though. Gothic horror reminds us of the darkness that our lives is in the shadow of. In classic gothic horror, particularly British/European style, we see the more classic motifs (the crumbling castles of the so-called \u2018dark ages\u2019 and with them the specters of ancient bloodshed &amp; tyranny as well as the barbaric warrior aristocrats, the decadent halls of cathedrals [most of these writers were Protestants, bear in mind] filled with false teachers who profaned the temple as well as wielding zealots crusaders and hawkish inquisitors; but in time even the more bourgeois elite in their country manors became wicked specters alongside robber barons and grounds worked by shackled serfs and haunted by hidden sin and ambitious devil deals). Some have argued that America doesn\u2019t have the proper environment for gothic horror but that also seems untrue now: gothic horror reflects its environment and it\u2019s its storytellers. American gothic took on its own unique characteristics (Victorian style manors and the later suburban mcmanors became the new domains of haunted houses which hid dark secrets from the civilized world, forests that lurked with terrible monsters [fueled by the paranoia of settler-colonists and their descendants about local indigenous peoples and wildlife alike], smooth talking tent revivalists who seduced innocent daughters and dour-faced Puritan witch hunters replaced Catholic institutions with homegrown Protestant alternatives, cities became living creatures which were infested with vice and violence and disease, while across the nations the original sins of genocide and slavery left unhealed scars which bled miasmic nightmares and haunting terrors). Gothic styles shifted to suit the time and environment but the past remained eternally alive within the shroud of the gothic world where the sins of yesterday still cried out in the shadowy places of today.<br /> <br /> \u2022Corruption &amp; Decay<br /> Like I said above about the Gothic Paradigm of sterility, the idea of horror as being the counterpoint or the failed state of reproductive forces also shows within the gothic paradigm. Not only does gothic horror show how the world can collapse - how not only your home or your life or your society but your very own body is a fragile thing which could dissolve into its base components at any moment. Gothic horror shows us the telltale marks of decay: how buildings sag under their own weight, how bridges rust further and further, how institutions become more infested with bribery and corruption, and how our own bodies slow and begin to become more and more like the death\u2019s head which we inevitably become. The dread which this decay manifests is a classic part of gothic horror principles, but when applied to society it also serves as social critique which dovetails neatly with punk. Gothic horror demonstrates corruption and perversion within social institutions - how governments which out to serve the people become the ministries of tyrants or oligarchs, how the clergy which ought to tend to parishioner souls becomes more concerned with Mammon and Scarlet Babylon, how militaries which out to defend ones nation turn into machines of blood profit and frenzied psychopathy, how through money or power or vice or whatever other weakness all things are drawn into a web of perversity and corruption. This also neatly plays into American Noir as being in part descended from Gothic Horror, as this philosophy of society remains clearly blazoned within the noir ethos.<br /> <br /> \u2022Transgression <br /> Part of the tragedy of gothic figures is that there dramatic tensions are defined by some sort of transgression, whether they are protagonist or villain. They hope for some sort of Eden or Paradise, whether that\u2019s a literally theological salvation or simply a fulfilled life; but they are withheld from happiness or fulfillment by transgression. You can see archetypes like this in classic figures like Gothic Satan who transgresses for pride and refuses to seek restitution even after being damned, Gothic Eve who transgresses from curiosity and once damned chooses to endure and follow her course, or Gothic Adam who transgresses by mistake and suffers in damnation while all the time striving for salvation. This idea of transgression as defining for gothic figures applies neatly for vampires as well: a vampire is a transgression against life and nature and as a consequence for the transgressive nature of their existence they are cursed to never live the fulfilled life possible for humanity and to ever be tormented by their monstrosity and the horrible ramifications it brings.<br /> <br /> These are just a few ideas briefly summarized, but I hope it shows how there\u2019s more to gothic themes then just a Tim Burton pastiche and that it\u2019s useful for folks interested in doing more gothic things with their games and stories.<br /> <br /> SOME BOOKS I READ<br /> \u2022Gothic Horror, Index of Gothic Horror Tropes, So You Want to Write a Gothic Horror story (TVTropes.com)<br /> \u2022The Biology of Horror (by Jack Morgan)<br /> \u2022The Gothic Vision (by Dani Caravallo)<br /> \u2022Journeys Into Darkness (by James Goho)<br /> \u2022GURPS Horror (Steve Jackson Games)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11637,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","user":"Gryffon15","date":". 12-03-2021, 06:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-03T16:36:41-08:00","id":1469540,"title":"","content":"I happen to enjoy using Brutalist architecture as a back drop, given its associations with the urban decay of the 70s and 80s, as well as with unfeeling and corrupt bureaucracies, being used as it was in government buildings and public housing projects. These massive slabs of concrete with bits of steel and glass seem to perfectly sum up the WoD in the latter half of the 20th century. But at the same time, some of them have this weird sort of stark and stoic feel (St. Basil's church in LA, for example), and more than a few are almost surreal and alien (Hotel de Lac in Tunis, which looks like someone turned a ziggurat pyramid on its head; Habitat 67 in Montreal). <br /> The Bauhaus school of architecture and design is another good one, with its simplicity and often industrial tones. Also the almost personality-less Neomodern style, and the aging grandeur of Art Deco.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-04T04:17:32-08:00","id":1469570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1469238-how-gothic-is-you-game?p=1469429#post1469429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I admit I tend to play Sabbat as mocking the whole Goth thing. They revel in their evil, feel no guilt, and could not care less about damnation. They love being monsters and all it cost them was everything.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Well my comment was tongue in cheek but I would say they feel guilt and care very much about damnation (their response to it is the issue of contention) Even if you go for the regression and complete lack of nuance which defines recent writings they still have the capacity to feel bad. If anything a bit of introspection and doubt makes then more disturbing and gothic","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 12-04-2021, 08:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-05T02:24:49-08:00","id":1469634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1469238-how-gothic-is-you-game?p=1469540#post1469540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Bauhaus school of architecture and design is another good one, with its simplicity and often industrial tones. Also the almost personality-less Neomodern style, and the aging grandeur of Art Deco.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel Most styles of Architecture can be used to say something about the place<br /> Gothic: Huge wealth divides between rich and poor (This is an expensive style) , that people used to adhere to a faith when now nobody has faith... <br /> (neo)classical: Elitist wankery <br /> Brutalist: Dreams that failed horribly. <br /> Modern: Soulless<br /> Art deco: times used to be better<br /> ..and so on and so forth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-05T14:38:00-08:00","id":1469666,"title":"","content":"I think that WoD is the quitessential &quot;dark and brooding&quot; fantasy-verse. <br /> <br /> Not because it is the darkest: it isn't.<br /> Actually it has the right amount of darkness and mistery to avoid darkness-induced apathy. It's very introspective.<br /> <br /> Warhammer is even more dark and more focused on almost-cartoonish violence.<br /> Kult is very esoteric and a little bit pretentious in my opinion.<br /> Call of Cthuluh focus on helpnessnes and horror, so much that introspection is obscured.<br /> Ravenloft is too combat-focused, and basically a vampire-themed d&amp;d.<br /> Cyperpunk is frantic, too frantic to delve deep in the brooding genre.<br /> <br /> <br /> Actually, the New World of Darkness is the most gothic, IMO. The old has many high-magic fantasy elements and less mistery.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27051-solomon-draak","name":"Solomon Draak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27051_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-06T12:58:52-08:00","id":1469759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1469238-how-gothic-is-you-game?p=1469634#post1469634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(neo)classical: Elitist wankery</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a marvellous summation of the V5 Camarilla and the appeal of playing within it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}